body:
Every distributed agent template `opencode-suite/agents/*.md` carries an opencode 2.x ordered `permissions` array of `{ action, resource, effect }` rules. opencode evaluates the ordered rule set; the plugin guide states that session-scoped rules are evaluated after the agent's rules with the last matching rule winning, and apg's templates rely on ordered rules with that precedence (a different precedence diverges the fs-tool scope from the `edit` scope). The action vocabulary is opencode 2.x's — `shell`, `subagent`, `edit`, and the apg-suite tool actions. The `mode` and `description` keys carry the agent's frontmatter, a variant joins the model reference as `provider/model#variant`, and the distributed hidden subagents carry `hidden: true`.

Each template's grant set:
- the `codebase-navigator` holds the `subagent` rules that name the distributed suite agents, the `*-implementer` agents, and the release-agent as dispatch targets, plus the apg-suite tool action rules;
- the `agent-builder` holds its main-checkout `edit` rules (`.opencode/agents/**`, `opencode.json`, `AGENTS.md`) and its exact read-only git verb set plus `git add`/`git commit` as `shell` rules;
- the `implementation-phase-reviewer` holds its read-only apg-suite, plan-read, and review rules, with the `question`/edit/scan/authoring rules absent (`domain.entity.distributed-agent-set`).

Acceptance criteria: every `opencode-suite/agents/*.md` file carries a `permissions` array whose entries name opencode 2.x actions and carry the agent's own grant set; each template enumerates its grant set so the set is checkable on its own; the `agent-builder.md` main-checkout `edit` rules and read-only git verb set are present.
